cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use eigenchip in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "eigenchip: reducing music to a few chip voices"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sandner
    given-names: Daniel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1041-814X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eigensoundlab/eigenchip"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
keywords:
  - music information retrieval
  - symbolic music
  - automatic music transcription
  - arrangement
  - voice reduction
  - chiptune
  - MIDI
abstract: >-
  A research toolkit for reducing polyphonic music to three or four monophonic
  voices playable by a simple chip synthesizer. Interchangeable arrangement
  strategies are compared on a fixed corpus with symbolic measures of how much
  melody, bass, harmony and rhythm survive the reduction. Sound files are
  read through interchangeable transcription baselines, measured on synthetic
  audio of the same corpus.
